`:DECLARE nCount :DEFAULT 0;` packs two statements into one: :DEFAULT
only follows :PARAMETERS, and a declaration takes no initializer. The
:DEFAULT keyword inside the :DECLARE list is reported once, by
diag.default_on_declare_line; diag.unexpected_token defers to it
(issue #323).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE StartCounter;
	:DECLARE nCount :DEFAULT 0;
	nCount := nCount + 1;
	:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE StartCounter;
	:DECLARE nCount :DEFAULT 0;

	nCount := nCount + 1;

	:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:18-2:26 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' cannot initialize a ':DECLARE' list - ':DECLARE' takes only names, so this does not compile; give the variable its value with an assignment on the next line
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:18-2:26 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' cannot initialize a ':DECLARE' list - ':DECLARE' takes only names, so this does not compile; give the variable its value with an assignment on the next line
